<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first establish the expression for <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\emptyset}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\emptyset}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and then derive the expected number of explorations in (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). To begin, let <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(t_{1},t_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(t_{1},t_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event that an option with a reward exceeding <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is identified during the time slots <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{1},\ldots,t_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{1},\ldots,t_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event that no agent has found an option with a reward greater than <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> by time <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, the events <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(0,t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(0,t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are complementary.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\emptyset}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\emptyset}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as the expected reward at time <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> for myopic agents under the full communication policy. Since the reward at time <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the exploration history up to <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we partition the history into the cases when no option exceeding <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> has been found (event <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>) and when at least one such option has been identified (event <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(0,t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(0,t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus, we can write</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big]=\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|\bar{E}_{t-1}\Big]+\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,t-1)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(0,t-1)}\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big]=\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|\bar{E}_{t-1}\Big]+\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,t-1)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(0,t-1)}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since all agents use an exploration threshold <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1}=\ldots=u_{t}=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}=\ldots=u_{t}=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, if no option with reward greater than <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> has been discovered (i.e., if <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs), then every agent explores at time <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and earns an expected reward of <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|\bar{E}_{t-1}\Big]=NF(\mu)^{Nt}\mu." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|\bar{E}_{t-1}\Big]=NF(\mu)^{Nt}\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Once an option with a reward greater than <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is found for the first time at some time <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, all agents cease further exploration. Thus, the event <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(0,t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(0,t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> can be decomposed as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{(0,t-1)}=E_{(0,0)}+\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=1}\bar{E}_{\tau-1}\cap E_{(\tau,\tau)}=\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}E_{(\tau,\tau)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{(0,t-1)}=E_{(0,0)}+\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=1}\bar{E}_{\tau-1}\cap E_{(\tau,\tau)}=\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}E_{(\tau,\tau)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we can express the contribution from <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(0,t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(0,t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,t-1)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(0,t-1)}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,t-1)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(0,t-1)}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\Big(\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big)\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\Big(\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big)\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Under the event <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(\tau,\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(\tau,\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>, an option with a reward greater than <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is identified by time <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and is subsequently selected for exploitation at any <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, and its value is not affected by exploration outcomes prior to <math id="A1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the expected social welfare at time <math id="A1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on <math id="A1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(\tau,\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(\tau,\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]=N\mathbb{E}\Big[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\{m_{n}(\tau)\}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]=N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]=N\mathbb{E}\Big[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}\{m_{n}(\tau)\}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]=N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting this back into the decomposition in (<a href="#A1.E27" title="In Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]=\left(\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\right)N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum^{N}_{n=1}r_{a_{n}(t)}\Big|E_{(\tau,\tau)}\Big]=\left(\sum^{t-1}_{\tau=0}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\right)N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-F(\mu)^{Nt})N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-F(\mu)^{Nt})N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">By summing (<a href="#A1.E26" title="In Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E28" title="In Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), we obtain the expected reward at time <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=NF(\mu)^{Nt}\mu+(1-F(\mu)^{Nt})N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=NF(\mu)^{Nt}\mu+(1-F(\mu)^{Nt})N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}-NF(\mu)^{Nt}\left(1-\mu-\int^{1}_{\mu}\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}dr\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}-NF(\mu)^{Nt}\left(1-\mu-\int^{1}_{\mu}\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}dr\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}-NF(\mu)^{Nt}\int^{1}_{\mu}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}dr." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=N\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}-NF(\mu)^{Nt}\int^{1}_{\mu}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Summing <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\emptyset}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\emptyset}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> over the entire time horizon, the total social welfare under the full communication policy is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\emptyset}=\sum^{T}_{t=0}v_{\emptyset}(t)=N(T+1)\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}-N\frac{1-F(\mu)^{N(T+1)}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}\int^{1}_{\mu}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}dr," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\emptyset}=\sum^{T}_{t=0}v_{\emptyset}(t)=N(T+1)\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}-N\frac{1-F(\mu)^{N(T+1)}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}\int^{1}_{\mu}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}dr,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof of (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\{1,\ldots,T+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\{1,\ldots,T+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the random variable representing the time at which myopic agents cease exploration under the full communication policy throughout the entire process. Then the expected exploration time is given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tau]=\sum^{T+1}_{t=1}t\mathbb{P}(\tau=t)=\sum^{T+1}_{t=1}\mathbb{P}(\tau\geq t)=\sum^{T+1}_{t=1}F(\mu)^{N(t-1)}=\frac{1-F(\mu)^{N(T+1)}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tau]=\sum^{T+1}_{t=1}t\mathbb{P}(\tau=t)=\sum^{T+1}_{t=1}\mathbb{P}(\tau\geq t)=\sum^{T+1}_{t=1}F(\mu)^{N(t-1)}=\frac{1-F(\mu)^{N(T+1)}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">where the second equality follows from the identity <math id="A1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tau]=\sum_{t\geq 1}\mathbb{P}(\tau\geq t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tau]=\sum_{t\geq 1}\mathbb{P}(\tau\geq t)</annotation></semantics></math> and the last equality results from summing the finite geometric series. This completes the proof of (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have shown that equation (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) is sufficient for the non-optimality of a full communication policy in the presence of myopic agents, as discussed in Section <a href="#S3" title="3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. It remains to demonstrate that (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) is also a necessary condition. To this end, consider equation (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.2. Decentralized Communication Mechanism ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) for <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> under any communication restriction mechanism. If <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;V_{\emptyset}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;V_{\emptyset}</annotation></semantics></math>, then at least one of the terms</p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(T-T_{m}-\Delta_{m})y_{\Delta_{m}+1}-\sum_{i=1}^{\Delta_{m}}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(T-T_{m}-\Delta_{m})y_{\Delta_{m}+1}-\sum_{i=1}^{\Delta_{m}}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{1,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{1,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math> must be positive. This implies that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(T-\Delta_{m})y_{\Delta_{m}+1}-\sum_{i=1}^{\Delta_{m}}x_{i}&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(T-\Delta_{m})y_{\Delta_{m}+1}-\sum_{i=1}^{\Delta_{m}}x_{i}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is exactly the condition given in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In Proposition 3.2. ‣ 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof for Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.2. Decentralized Communication Mechanism ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we prove the expressions for <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) for the special communication restriction mechanism <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathcal{M}}=\{T_{1},\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathcal{M}}=\{T_{1},\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which features a single no-communication window. Next, we extend the result to the general case as stated in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.2. Decentralized Communication Mechanism ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. In particular, we first prove the expression for <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.2. Decentralized Communication Mechanism ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), and then we establish the formula for the expected number of exploration time slots in (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In Lemma 3.3. ‣ 3.2. Decentralized Communication Mechanism ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(t_{1},t_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(t_{1},t_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, we introduce <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{n}_{(t_{1},t_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{n}_{(t_{1},t_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}^{n}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}^{n}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, customizing these events for a specific agent <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> as required for the analysis in this section. We introduce the following two lemmas:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma C.1.</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the event <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1,\ldots,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1,\ldots,M</annotation></semantics></math>, in which an option with a reward higher than <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is identified during the no-communication interval <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for the long-term exploitation of all myopic agents, the expected maximum reward discovered after this window is<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">3</span></span>
                
                
                
              <span id="footnote3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">Note that communication always occurs after selecting an action at each time slot. Although the no-communication time window is defined as </span><math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta-1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">, the action chosen at time </span><math id="footnote3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}+\Delta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}+\Delta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> is also under no-communication, resulting in the same impact of communication restriction as for </span><math id="footnote3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta-1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m}+\Delta_{m})|E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m}+\Delta_{m})|E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{m}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{m}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the event <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that no agent discovers an option with a reward higher than <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> during the time interval from 0 to <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event that exactly <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> agents find an option with a reward exceeding <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> within the window <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the event <math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}</annotation></semantics></math> can be further decomposed as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}=\sum^{N}_{k=1}b_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}=\sum^{N}_{k=1}b_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m}+\Delta_{m})|E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m}+\Delta_{m})|E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})}]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum^{N}_{k=1}\mathbb{P}(b_{k})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m}+\Delta_{m})|b_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum^{N}_{k=1}\mathbb{P}(b_{k})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m}+\Delta_{m})|b_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{N}F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}(1-F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1})^{k}F(\mu)^{(\Delta_{m}+1)(N-k)}\begin{pmatrix}N\\
k\end{pmatrix}\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>N</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>k</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{N}F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}(1-F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1})^{k}F(\mu)^{(\Delta_{m}+1)(N-k)}\begin{pmatrix}N\\
k\end{pmatrix}\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\left(\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}(1-F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1})\right)+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1}\right)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{m}+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\left(\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}(1-F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1})\right)+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1}\right)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{m}+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(31)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{m}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\mu)^{NT_{m}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{m}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{m}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma C.2.</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under event <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1,\dots,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1,\dots,M</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m+1}&gt;T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m+1}&gt;T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1</annotation></semantics></math>, an option yielding a reward greater than <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is identified and exploited by all myopic agents during the interval <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,\dots,T_{m+1}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,\dots,T_{m+1}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m+1}=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m+1}=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1</annotation></semantics></math>, this event has probability zero and cannot occur. The expected maximum reward discovered after this interval is therefore given by:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(32)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m+1}-1)|E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m+1}-1)|E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(F(\mu)^{N(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1)}-F(\mu)^{NT_{m+1}})\int_{\mu}^{1}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(F(\mu)^{N(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1)}-F(\mu)^{NT_{m+1}})\int_{\mu}^{1}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which equals 0 when <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m+1}=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m+1}=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, this expression applies for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by the mechanism.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">In communication time window <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\in\{T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,,\ldots,T_{m+1}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\{T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,,\ldots,T_{m+1}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, all agents will immediately stop exploration at time <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> under event <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m+1}-1)|E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(T_{m+1}-1)|E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)}]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum^{T_{m+1}-1}_{\tau=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(\tau)|E_{(\tau,\tau)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum^{T_{m+1}-1}_{\tau=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\mathbb{E}[\max_{n\in\mathcal{N}}m_{n}(\tau)|E_{(\tau,\tau)}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum^{T_{m+1}-1}_{\tau=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\int^{1}_{\mu}dr\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum^{T_{m+1}-1}_{\tau=T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1}\mathbb{P}(E_{(\tau,\tau)})\int^{1}_{\mu}dr\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(F(\mu)^{N(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1)}-F(\mu)^{NT_{m+1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(F(\mu)^{N(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1)}-F(\mu)^{NT_{m+1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Under the communication restriction mechanism <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathcal{M}}=\{T_{1},\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathcal{M}}=\{T_{1},\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total time slots can be segmented into three time windows as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(33)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{0,\ldots,T_{1}\},\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\},\{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{0,\ldots,T_{1}\},\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\},\{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The expected social welfare <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> under mechanism <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> depends on which time window in (<a href="#A3.E33" title="In Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) the time <math id="A3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to. We analyze <math id="A3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> separately for each window. For <math id="A3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\dots,T_{1}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\dots,T_{1}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected social welfare <math id="A3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> matches the welfare under full communication, <math id="A3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\emptyset}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\emptyset}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E29" title="In Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), because both mechanisms share the same historical event space during this interval.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the historical events preceding <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for agent <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> are categorized as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(34)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{1}-1)},E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)},\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{1}-1)},E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)},\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">under which <math id="A3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(35)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\sum_{n=1}^{N}r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]+\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}]+\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\sum_{n=1}^{N}r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]+\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}]+\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.3" class="ltx_p">where the component <math id="A3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\sum_{n=1}^{N}r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\sum_{n=1}^{N}r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]</annotation></semantics></math>, signifying the expected reward for long-term exploitation under event <math id="A3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, can be directly generalized from (<a href="#A1.E28" title="In Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(36)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\sum_{n=1}^{N}r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]=N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[\sum_{n=1}^{N}r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]=N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.4" class="ltx_p">Regarding the component <math id="A3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}]</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E35" title="In Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), the event <math id="A3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that agent <math id="A3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> independently discovers an option with a reward exceeding <math id="A3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, leading to the following expected reward for exploitation:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(37)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}]=\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}=F(\mu)^{NT_{1}}(1-F(\mu)^{t-T_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)}]=\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{1},t-1)})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}=F(\mu)^{NT_{1}}(1-F(\mu)^{t-T_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.5" class="ltx_p">Conversely, under the event <math id="A3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}_{t-1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}_{t-1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, agent <math id="A3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> must choose exploration at time <math id="A3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding an expected reward of <math id="A3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mu)^{Nt}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mu)^{Nt}\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these three components, we compute <math id="A3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{1}+1,\dots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{1}+1,\dots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}(1-F(\mu)^{t-T_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}+t-T_{1}}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}(1-F(\mu)^{t-T_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}+t-T_{1}}\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+F(\mu)^{N(t-T_{1})}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}\right)-\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{t-T_{1}}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+F(\mu)^{N(t-T_{1})}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}\right)-\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{t-T_{1}}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)-NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}x_{t-T_{1}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)-NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}x_{t-T_{1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-T_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-T_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we examine <math id="A3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for</p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where the historical events preceding <math id="A3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> are categorized as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex37X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{1}-1)},\;E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})},\;E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)},\;\bar{E}_{t-1},\quad\text{if }t&gt;T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{1}-1)},\;E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})},\;E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)},\;\bar{E}_{t-1},\quad\text{if }t&gt;T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{1}-1)},\;E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})},\;\bar{E}_{t-1},\quad\text{if }t=T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{1}-1)},\;E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})},\;\bar{E}_{t-1},\quad\text{if }t=T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.3" class="ltx_p">where the expected reward for exploitation associated with <math id="A3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}],</annotation></semantics></math>
is given in (<a href="#A3.E36" title="In Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>). Similarly, the expected reward for exploitation related to <math id="A3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid E_{(T_{1},T_{1}+\Delta_{1})}],</annotation></semantics></math>
is provided in (<a href="#A3.E30" title="In Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>. Additionally, conditioned on the event <math id="A3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{E}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{E}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected reward at time <math id="A3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the exploration reward <math id="A3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives</p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid\bar{E}_{t-1}]=F(\mu)^{Nt}\mu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid\bar{E}_{t-1}]=F(\mu)^{Nt}\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.4" class="ltx_p">It remains to assess the expected reward for exploitation under the event <math id="A3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be directly generalized from (<a href="#A3.E32" title="In Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> (since <math id="A3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1</annotation></semantics></math>) as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(38)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)}]=\bigl(F(\mu)^{N(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1)}-F(\mu)^{Nt}\bigr)\int^{1}_{\mu}r\,d\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}\mid E_{(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,t-1)}]=\bigl(F(\mu)^{N(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1)}-F(\mu)^{Nt}\bigr)\int^{1}_{\mu}r\,d\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.5" class="ltx_p">By combining (<a href="#A3.E36" title="In Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E30" title="In Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) with <math id="A3.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{m}=T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{m}=T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{m}=\Delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{m}=\Delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mu)^{Nt}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mu)^{Nt}\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, and (<a href="#A3.E38" title="In Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>), we derive the final form of <math id="A3.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="A3.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T\}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{1}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{1}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{1}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{1}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+N(F(\mu)^{N(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1)}-F(\mu)^{Nt})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{Nt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+N(F(\mu)^{N(T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1)}-F(\mu)^{Nt})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{Nt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{1}+1)}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}\right)-\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{1}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{1}+1)}\frac{1-F(r)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}\right)-\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{1}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}y_{\Delta_{1}+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}y_{\Delta_{1}+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{{\Delta_{1}}+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{{\Delta_{1}}+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is given in (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>). Integrate <math id="A3.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in different time window, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=\begin{cases}v_{\emptyset}(t),&amp;\text{if }t=1,\ldots,T_{1},\\
v_{\emptyset}(t)-NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}x_{t-T_{1}},&amp;\text{if }t=T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1},\\
v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}y_{\Delta_{1}+1},&amp;\text{if }t=T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=\begin{cases}v_{\emptyset}(t),&amp;\text{if }t=1,\ldots,T_{1},\\
v_{\emptyset}(t)-NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}x_{t-T_{1}},&amp;\text{if }t=T_{1}+1,\ldots,T_{1}+\Delta_{1},\\
v_{\emptyset}(t)+NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}y_{\Delta_{1}+1},&amp;\text{if }t=T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1,\ldots,T.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.7" class="ltx_p">Then, the social welfare for total time horizon <math id="A3.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum^{T_{1}}_{t=0}v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)+\sum^{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}}_{t=T_{1}+1}v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)+\sum^{T}_{t=T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1}v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=V_{\emptyset}+N(T-T_{1}-\Delta_{1})F(\mu)^{NT_{1}}y_{\Delta_{1}+1}-NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\sum^{\Delta_{1}}_{t=1}x_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum^{T_{1}}_{t=0}v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)+\sum^{T_{1}+\Delta_{1}}_{t=T_{1}+1}v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)+\sum^{T}_{t=T_{1}+\Delta_{1}+1}v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)=V_{\emptyset}+N(T-T_{1}-\Delta_{1})F(\mu)^{NT_{1}}y_{\Delta_{1}+1}-NF(\mu)^{NT_{1}}\sum^{\Delta_{1}}_{t=1}x_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.8" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof of (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1. Analysis of Existing Centralized Communication Policy ‣ 3. Decentralized Communication Mechanism for Myopic Agents ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we consider the expected reward <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> for general communication restriction mechanism <math id="A3.p9.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\cup_{m=1}^{M}\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\cup_{m=1}^{M}\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Generalizing from (<a href="#A3.E34" title="In Appendix C Proof for Lemma ‣ Human-in-the-loop Learning Through Decentralized Communication Mechanisms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>), when <math id="A3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> falls within <math id="A3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the historical events can be partitioned as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{m}-1)},E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})},E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)},\ldots,E^{n}_{(T_{m},t-1)},\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{(0,T_{m}-1)},E_{(T_{m},T_{m}+\Delta_{m})},E_{(T_{m}+\Delta_{m}+1,T_{m+1}-1)},\ldots,E^{n}_{(T_{m},t-1)},\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.2" class="ltx_p">under which <math id="A3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{T_{m},\ldots,T_{m}+\Delta_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\mathcal{M}}(t)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\mathcal{M}}(t)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]+\sum^{m-1}_{i=1}N\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{i},T_{i}+\Delta_{1})})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(T_{i},T_{i}+\Delta_{1})}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N\mathbb{P}(E_{(0,T_{1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(0,T_{1}-1)}]+\sum^{m-1}_{i=1}N\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{i},T_{i}+\Delta_{1})})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(T_{i},T_{i}+\Delta_{1})}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(39)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum^{m-1}_{i=1}N\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{i}+\Delta_{i}+1,T_{i+1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(T_{i}+\Delta_{i}+1,T_{i+1}-1)})]+\sum^{N}_{n=1}(\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{m},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{m},t-1)}]+\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1}])," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>N</mi><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum^{m-1}_{i=1}N\mathbb{P}(E_{(T_{i}+\Delta_{i}+1,T_{i+1}-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E_{(T_{i}+\Delta_{i}+1,T_{i+1}-1)})]+\sum^{N}_{n=1}(\mathbb{P}(E^{n}_{(T_{m},t-1)})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|E^{n}_{(T_{m},t-1)}]+\mathbb{P}(\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1})\mathbb{E}[r_{a_{n}(t)}|\bar{E}^{n}_{t-1}]),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.3" class="ltx_p">where each part can be directly generalized from the derivation of <math id="A3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\bar{\mathcal{M}}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{\mathcal{M}}(t)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{\mathcal{M}}(t)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{m}}(1-F(\mu)^{t-T_{m}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{NT_{m}+t-T_{m}}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N(1-F(\mu)^{NT_{1}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)^{N}-F(\mu)^{N}}{1-F(\mu)^{N}}+NF(\mu)^{NT_{m}}(1-F(\mu)^{t-T_{m}})\int^{1}_{\mu}rd\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{NT_{m}+t-T_{m}}\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+N\sum^{m-1}_{i=1}F(\mu)^{NT_{i}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{i}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{i}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+N\sum^{m-1}_{i=1}F(\mu)^{NT_{i}}\left(1-\mu F(\mu)^{N(\Delta_{i}+1)}-\int^{1}_{\mu}\left(\frac{F(r)-F(\mu)}{1-F(\mu)}+F(\mu)^{\Delta_{i}+1}\frac{1-F(r)}{1-F(\mu)}\right)^{N}dr\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
